    "class": "fixture_lifecycle_misuse",
    "source_established": "The fixture sets total V2 max_concurrent_threads_per_session=3. Production reserves one root slot, leaving child residency capacity 2. Worker and grandchild occupy those child slots. Sibling admission can synchronously unload a completed eligible child, remove its live recorder and manager entry, while a previously acquired Arc<CodexThread> remains held by the fixture. The old worker flush was after sibling admission and could therefore use a handle whose recorder had already been revoked. The moved flush restores the required live-owner ordering without changing residency policy.",
